Basic EIGRP Configuration
R1
router eigrp 100
 eigrp router-id 1.1.1.1
 network 10.12.12.0 0.0.0.3
R2
router eigrp 100
 eigrp router-id 2.2.2.2
 network 10.12.12.0 0.0.0.3

The 10.12.12.0/30 network provides the Layer 3 connection used to form the EIGRP adjacency between R1 and R2.

Loopbacks

Loopback interfaces are used for router identification and for testing route advertisement.

R1
interface loopback0
 ip address 1.1.1.1 255.255.255.255

interface loopback1
 ip address 11.11.11.1 255.255.255.255
R2
interface loopback0
 ip address 2.2.2.2 255.255.255.255

interface loopback1
 ip address 22.22.22.2 255.255.255.255
Passive Interfaces

Loopback interfaces can be advertised through EIGRP without forming EIGRP neighbor adjacencies.

R1
router eigrp 100
 passive-interface loopback0
 passive-interface loopback1
R2
router eigrp 100
 passive-interface loopback0
 passive-interface loopback1

The loopback networks remain advertised by EIGRP, but EIGRP Hellos are not sent through the loopback interfaces.

EIGRP Stub

R1 can be configured as an EIGRP stub router.

R1(config)#router eigrp 100
R1(config-router)#eigrp stub

This identifies R1 as a stub router and limits the types of routes it advertises to its EIGRP neighbor.

EIGRP Summarization

R1 summarizes its 11.11.11.1/32 network toward R2.

Summary network:

11.11.11.0/29

Configuration:

R1(config)#interface GigabitEthernet0/0
R1(config-if)#ip summary-address eigrp 100 11.11.11.0 255.255.255.248

This allows R1 to advertise the summarized 11.11.11.0/29 prefix toward R2 instead of advertising the individual 11.11.11.1/32 route.

EIGRP Authentication

EIGRP authentication is configured using a key chain.

Key Chain
key chain EIGRP-KEY
 key 1
  key-string CCNP
R1
interface GigabitEthernet0/0
 ip authentication key-chain eigrp 100 EIGRP-KEY
 ip authentication mode eigrp 100 md5
R2
interface GigabitEthernet0/0
 ip authentication key-chain eigrp 100 EIGRP-KEY
 ip authentication mode eigrp 100 md5

Both sides of the EIGRP adjacency must use matching authentication settings and key information.

