The topology table can be used to examine these values and determine why EIGRP selects a particular path.

EIGRP Variance

EIGRP variance can be used to allow unequal-cost load balancing.

Example:

router eigrp 100
 variance 2

The variance value multiplies the feasible distance of the successor and determines whether additional paths can be installed as feasible unequal-cost paths.

EIGRP and OSPF Redistribution

R2 acts as the redistribution point between EIGRP AS 100 and OSPF.

EIGRP → OSPF
router ospf 1
 redistribute eigrp 100 subnets
OSPF → EIGRP
router eigrp 100
 redistribute ospf 1 metric 10000 100 255 1 1500

The redistribution configuration allows routes learned through EIGRP to be introduced into OSPF and routes learned through OSPF to be introduced into EIGRP.

