R1 and R2 use EIGRP AS 100 to provide dynamic routing across the 10.12.12.0/30 transit network.

Loopback interfaces provide stable router identifiers and test networks. Passive interfaces allow the loopback networks to be advertised without attempting to form EIGRP adjacencies.

R1 demonstrates EIGRP stub routing and route summarization, while EIGRP authentication secures the adjacency between R1 and R2.

R2 also functions as the routing boundary between EIGRP AS 100 and the OSPF domain, allowing route redistribution between the two routing protocols.
